<figure class="pw-figure" data-wal-checkpoint aria-labelledby="pw-checkpoint-title">
  <figcaption id="pw-checkpoint-title"><span>Figure 2</span><strong>The redo point is earlier than checkpoint completion</strong></figcaption>
  <div class="pw-history"><div>Previous checkpoint<br/><b>Old redo point</b></div><div class="pw-new-redo">New checkpoint starts<br/><b>R · new redo point</b></div><div>Writes continue<br/><b>Later changes</b></div><div class="pw-completion">Checkpoint finishes<br/><b>K · checkpoint record</b></div></div>
  <div class="pw-page-pair"><div><strong>Products page A</strong><span data-page-a data-live></span></div><div><strong>Another page B</strong><span data-page-b data-live></span></div></div>
  <p class="pw-result">Restart can safely use: <strong data-redo data-live></strong></p>
  <p class="pw-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite"></p>
  <div class="pw-controls" role="group" aria-label="Playback for figure 2"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step></span><div data-hold><span></span></div></div>
  <p class="pw-caption">A conceptual checkpoint on a writing primary. R and K are symbolic positions in WAL, not timestamps or measured positions. Only two pages are drawn. Completion establishes the earlier R as safe; it does not promise that every change made before K is already in a data file.</p>
  <details><summary>Figure as text</summary><ol><li>The last completed checkpoint still supplies the safe redo point.</li><li>A new checkpoint establishes R and begins its required page writes.</li><li>The products page is written; page B still needs its required write.</li><li>A later price change dirties the products page again. Page B is written.</li><li>The checkpoint completes and records R. Restart can begin there even though later changes to the products page remain dirty.</li></ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
  import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-wal-checkpoint]').forEach(root=>{
    const states=[
      ['Dirty · earlier changes pending','Dirty · earlier changes pending','Old redo point','The previous completed checkpoint remains the recovery starting point. The new checkpoint has not begun.'],
      ['Required write pending','Required write pending','Old redo point','The new checkpoint chooses redo point R. It has work to finish before restart can rely on R.'],
      ['Required page written · sync pending','Required write pending','Old redo point','The checkpointer writes the products page. It must still complete the other required writes and synchronisation.'],
      ['Dirty again · changes after R','Required page written · sync pending','Old redo point','Writing continues during the checkpoint. A later change dirties the products page again. The required page writes still need synchronisation before the checkpoint can complete.'],
      ['Dirty · later changes covered by WAL','Required changes synchronised','R · new redo point','The checkpoint completes at K and records R. Recovery can start at R and redo later changes. K is not a promise that all pages contain every change up to K.']
    ];
    stepper(root,{steps:()=>states.length,draw:(step:number)=>{
      const s=states[step];
      root.querySelector('[data-page-a]')!.textContent=s[0];root.querySelector('[data-page-b]')!.textContent=s[1];root.querySelector('[data-redo]')!.textContent=s[2];root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=s[3];
      root.classList.toggle('pw-started',step>=1);root.classList.toggle('pw-done',step===4);
    }});
  });
</script>
